thinking
**Analyzing persistent git dirty state**

The run log updates with every command, causing repeated git status changes and commits; this may require committing after every command, including commits themselves, leading to a potentially endless commit loop.
thinking
**Mapping run log update conflicts with commit verification**

The run log updates after nearly every command, making it impossible to fully confirm a clean working tree post-commit without triggering new modifications; committing the log last and then avoiding further commands is the only practical approach despite strict confirmation requirements.
thinking
**Committing final run log changes and stopping command runs**

Planning to stage and commit the latest run log modifications now, then stop running further commands to avoid new log updates; the final response will reference the previously captured git show output and note this slight deviation.
